## 9. Isochrone Generation

An isochrone represents the spatial distribution
of excess porewater pressure at a given time factor.

The visualization example is located at:

`examples/consolidation_1d_example.py`

The following time factors are represented:

| Time Factor | Interpretation |
|---|---|
| 0.01 | Early consolidation |
| 0.02 | Early consolidation |
| 0.05 | Developing consolidation |
| 0.10 | Developing consolidation |
| 0.20 | Intermediate consolidation |
| 0.50 | Advanced consolidation |
| 1.00 | Near-complete consolidation |
| 2.00 | Very small remaining excess pressure |

These descriptions are qualitative.

The numerical values do not represent fixed
elapsed times without specifying $c_v$ and
$H_{dr}$.

### Generate the figure

From the repository root:

```bash
python examples/consolidation_1d_example.py
```

The output is saved to:

`outputs/terzaghi_1d_isochrones.png`

